Hello.
I am working with a commonfactor model with 3 phenotypes – ph1, ph2 and ph3. I
am using the userGWAS function to avoid problems with negative residual
variance for the phenotype ph1.
The model:
model <- “F1 =~ph1+ph2+ph3
F1~SNP
ph1~~a*ph1
a >.001”

Usermodel
<- userGWAS(covstruc = input1, SNPs=input2, estimation =”ML”, model=model,
modelchi=T, GC=”none”, sub=c(“F1~SNP”), printwarn=T)

I now want
to obtain heterogeneity (Q) index as described in the tutorial “Optional step
5: Run a follow-up model to obtain heterogeneity (Q) index)”. I have defined
the following “independent pathways” model:

model <-
”F1 =~ph1+ph2+ph3
ph1+ph2+ph3~SNP
ph1~~a*ph1
a>.001”

Usermodel
<- userGWAS(covstruc=input1, SNPs = input2, estimation = “ML”, model=model,
modelchi = T, GC = “none”, sub = c(“ph1+ph2+ph3~SNP”), printwarn = T)

When I run
the “independent pathways” model above, I receive an empty table as result. I
am not sure, if it is the model, that is defined incorrectly or if it is the
wrong component of the model (sub=(“ph1+ph2+ph3~SNP”)), I request. Can you help
me with this issue?

Thank you, Trine

